{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kn4DPx7MgMFWAfT1i53hBy","type":"tool_result","content":"5:Proposed — 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35. The transport, the identity and the slicing of B35 are decided by the amendment at the end (2026-11-09). No IPC, cache API/schema, daemon lifecycle,\n6-platform default or policy is implemented/adopted by this proposal. Reconcile and\n7-resolve the structural contract before functional start. Preserve accepted ADRs\n8-for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the\n9-MCP-Conductor-Harness validation boundary.\n10-\n11-## Context\n12-\n13-The [performance analysis](../reports/2026-10-12-pose-front-08-resident-performance.md)\n14-separates computation, transport and freshness costs. CLI-backed Store adapters\n15-spawn the binary with a fixed deadline; MCP persistence alone does not remove\n16-repeated algorithms or graph copies. The [UX analysis](../reports/2026-10-12-pose-front-07-operational-ux.md)\n17-shows plan/context composition and planning handoff gaps while P15 read parity\n18-already works. The [consistency analysis](../reports/2026-10-12-pose-front-09-consistency-recovery.md)\n19-identifies nested mutable aliasing and generation/coordination boundaries.\n20-\n21-Cached graph copies include shallow Nodes.Attributes, misses are not coordinated\n22-per key, and the single last graph can churn across projects. These are code-founded\n23-observations, not measured corruption by a current consumer or a native race.\n24-A client-owned MCP stdio stream cannot be attached by an unrelated CLI. Existing\n25-sessions/cursors/registry mutexes do not prove worktree IPC or write serialization.\n26-\n27-## Decision\n28-\n29-Propose these boundaries for review, without choosing wire/schema details yet:\n30-\n31-- Extract one typed domain interface for admitted operations. CLI/MCP adapt syntax\n32-  and rendering, with common results/coverage/generation/error semantics. Preserve\n33-  the adapter-not-fork principle; remove the POSE subprocess only where extraction\n34-  is qualified. Legitimate scoped Git and external Harness execution remain separate.\n35-- Preserve project selection and actual authority/assurance. Read-only planning or\n36-  typed CLI handoff does not authorize writes; sharing code, process UID or stdio\n37-  does not create Execution Identity, signature or human presence. Active-context\n38-  discovery keeps authorized logical IDs and never reveals unauthorized roots.\n39-- Keep validation orchestration outside arbitrary tools/call execution. Native\n40-  structural/read-only evaluations and explicitly admitted operations use the\n41-  domain; project check execution still requires its existing request/approval/\n42-  Harness contract. Scheduling, agents, workflow retries and notifications stay\n43-  outside the POSE core. Bounded admission/in-flight work here is evaluation of\n44-  requested calls, not a durable workflow queue or an autonomous scheduler.\n45-- Expose effectively immutable graph views or deep defensive copies at mutable\n--\n241:Decided 2026-11-09 with the maintainer, before the functional start of B35:\n242-\n243-- **Transport.** A stream socket in the user's own directory: a Unix domain socket\n244-  (Linux, macOS), mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user, whose peer is\n245-  checked by the operating system's credentials (`SO_PEERCRED`, `LOCAL_PEERCRED`)\n246-  before any byte is read. No TCP, no token, no network surface. Windows has no\n247-  named-pipe implementation in this repository (the standard library has none and\n248-  the repository takes no dependency for it): the runtime reports itself\n249-  unsupported there and every command runs standalone. That is a declared\n250-  limitation, not a silent one, and a named pipe with the owner's ACL is the\n251-  follow-up that lifts it.\n252-- **Identity.** user (uid) + canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) + Git common\n253-  directory + engine version/build + wire protocol + schema. The endpoint name is\n254-  a digest of the location part only (user, worktree, Git common directory), so two\n255-  worktrees or two users never share an endpoint; the engine part is compared at the\n256-  handshake, field by field, and a difference is refused naming it, so that a new CLI\n257-  that finds an old process after an update is refused by name instead of being\n258-  given a different endpoint and never learning the old one is there.\n259-- **Authority.** The runtime of slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers\n260-  handshake, status and stop. It confers no authority, signature or presence, and a\n261-  client that attaches gains nothing it did not have standalone.\n262-- **Slicing.** B35 is delivered in three specs, each reviewed on its own:\n263-  `pose-optional-worktree-runtime` (identity, endpoint, handshake, lifecycle,\n264-  standalone fallback: R1-R4), `pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache` (R5, R7: the\n265-  resident reuse of the B33 views, reconciliation, typed results) and\n266-  `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement` (R6, R8: budgets, short queries\n267-  protected from heavy checks, measured thresholds). Budgets and thresholds are\n268-  fixed from a measured synthetic corpus with a declared environment, never from a\n269-  historical sample."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"2c3f5902-424f-4def-acf6-70124fd65f08","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:37:57.650Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"5:Proposed — 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35. The transport, the identity and the slicing of B35 are decided by the amendment at the end (2026-11-09). No IPC, cache API/schema, daemon lifecycle,\n6-platform default or policy is implemented/adopted by this proposal. Reconcile and\n7-resolve the structural contract before functional start. Preserve accepted ADRs\n8-for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the\n9-MCP-Conductor-Harness validation boundary.\n10-\n11-## Context\n12-\n13-The [performance analysis](../reports/2026-10-12-pose-front-08-resident-performance.md)\n14-separates computation, transport and freshness costs. CLI-backed Store adapters\n15-spawn the binary with a fixed deadline; MCP persistence alone does not remove\n16-repeated algorithms or graph copies. The [UX analysis](../reports/2026-10-12-pose-front-07-operational-ux.md)\n17-shows plan/context composition and planning handoff gaps while P15 read parity\n18-already works. The [consistency analysis](../reports/2026-10-12-pose-front-09-consistency-recovery.md)\n19-identifies nested mutable aliasing and generation/coordination boundaries.\n20-\n21-Cached graph copies include shallow Nodes.Attributes, misses are not coordinated\n22-per key, and the single last graph can churn across projects. These are code-founded\n23-observations, not measured corruption by a current consumer or a native race.\n24-A client-owned MCP stdio stream cannot be attached by an unrelated CLI. Existing\n25-sessions/cursors/registry mutexes do not prove worktree IPC or write serialization.\n26-\n27-## Decision\n28-\n29-Propose these boundaries for review, without choosing wire/schema details yet:\n30-\n31-- Extract one typed domain interface for admitted operations. CLI/MCP adapt syntax\n32-  and rendering, with common results/coverage/generation/error semantics. Preserve\n33-  the adapter-not-fork principle; remove the POSE subprocess only where extraction\n34-  is qualified. Legitimate scoped Git and external Harness execution remain separate.\n35-- Preserve project selection and actual authority/assurance. Read-only planning or\n36-  typed CLI handoff does not authorize writes; sharing code, process UID or stdio\n37-  does not create Execution Identity, signature or human presence. Active-context\n38-  discovery keeps authorized logical IDs and never reveals unauthorized roots.\n39-- Keep validation orchestration outside arbitrary tools/call execution. Native\n40-  structural/read-only evaluations and explicitly admitted operations use the\n41-  domain; project check execution still requires its existing request/approval/\n42-  Harness contract. Scheduling, agents, workflow retries and notifications stay\n43-  outside the POSE core. Bounded admission/in-flight work here is evaluation of\n44-  requested calls, not a durable workflow queue or an autonomous scheduler.\n45-- Expose effectively immutable graph views or deep defensive copies at mutable\n--\n241:Decided 2026-11-09 with the maintainer, before the functional start of B35:\n242-\n243-- **Transport.** A stream socket in the user's own directory: a Unix domain socket\n244-  (Linux, macOS), mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user, whose peer is\n245-  checked by the operating system's credentials (`SO_PEERCRED`, `LOCAL_PEERCRED`)\n246-  before any byte is read. No TCP, no token, no network surface. Windows has no\n247-  named-pipe implementation in this repository (the standard library has none and\n248-  the repository takes no dependency for it): the runtime reports itself\n249-  unsupported there and every command runs standalone. That is a declared\n250-  limitation, not a silent one, and a named pipe with the owner's ACL is the\n251-  follow-up that lifts it.\n252-- **Identity.** user (uid) + canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) + Git common\n253-  directory + engine version/build + wire protocol + schema. The endpoint name is\n254-  a digest of the location part only (user, worktree, Git common directory), so two\n255-  worktrees or two users never share an endpoint; the engine part is compared at the\n256-  handshake, field by field, and a difference is refused naming it, so that a new CLI\n257-  that finds an old process after an update is refused by name instead of being\n258-  given a different endpoint and never learning the old one is there.\n259-- **Authority.** The runtime of slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers\n260-  handshake, status and stop. It confers no authority, signature or presence, and a\n261-  client that attaches gains nothing it did not have standalone.\n262-- **Slicing.** B35 is delivered in three specs, each reviewed on its own:\n263-  `pose-optional-worktree-runtime` (identity, endpoint, handshake, lifecycle,\n264-  standalone fallback: R1-R4), `pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache` (R5, R7: the\n265-  resident reuse of the B33 views, reconciliation, typed results) and\n266-  `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement` (R6, R8: budgets, short queries\n267-  protected from heavy checks, measured thresholds). Budgets and thresholds are\n268-  fixed from a measured synthetic corpus with a declared environment, never from a\n269-  historical sample.","numLines":71,"totalLines":71},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kn4DPx7MgMFWAfT1i53hBy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
