{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtEZHnjtGYHKqwB5uZcB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017hw9R5mer3yKodG11rpkGQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '946p' /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1986613151/worktree/POSE.md","description":"Print the runtime paragraph of the manual"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6570,"cache_read_input_tokens":55957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6570},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"234b5735-3856-4f9c-aa1a-6a80fac5f90f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:37:59.650Z","request_id":"req_011CgtEZHbLN7uJsoc8QFU8z","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017hw9R5mer3yKodG11rpkGQ":{"command":"sed -n '946p' /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1986613151/worktree/POSE.md","description":"Print the runtime paragraph of the manual"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017hw9R5mer3yKodG11rpkGQ","type":"tool_result","content":"**Optional worktree runtime.** `pose runtime start` starts, detached, a runtime for this worktree; `attach` and `status` handshake with it, `stop` drains it (`--drain <d>`, default 5s) and says how many requests in flight finished and how many were abandoned, `restart` is stop then start, and `serve` runs it in the foreground (`--idle <d>`, default 30m, stops an idle runtime; 0 never does). It is opt-in: no other command starts it, and every command runs standalone whether it runs or not. The runtime is identified by the user, the canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) and the Git common directory, so two worktrees of one repository, or two users, never share one; the handshake compares the engine, build, protocol and schema as well and an attach from another engine is refused naming the field. Its endpoint is a Unix domain socket (Linux, macOS) of mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user (`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pose`, else `pose-runtime-<uid>` under the temporary directory, or `POSE_RUNTIME_DIR`), whose peer the operating system identifies before a byte is read; a link, a loose mode, another owner or a file that is not a socket is refused, and a socket nobody answers on is replaced. There is no TCP and no token. Slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers handshake, status and stop, confers no authority, signature or presence, and every restart has a new epoch, inheriting nothing. On Windows, which has no named-pipe implementation here, `status` reports `unsupported` and every command runs standalone. `status` exits 0 for running, standalone and unsupported and 1 for an incompatible runtime; `attach` also exits 1 when there is nothing to attach to. `--json` prints the document `pose.runtime.status/1`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"5d07736f-d694-4efd-8d9d-926727160f3c","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:37:59.667Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"**Optional worktree runtime.** `pose runtime start` starts, detached, a runtime for this worktree; `attach` and `status` handshake with it, `stop` drains it (`--drain <d>`, default 5s) and says how many requests in flight finished and how many were abandoned, `restart` is stop then start, and `serve` runs it in the foreground (`--idle <d>`, default 30m, stops an idle runtime; 0 never does). It is opt-in: no other command starts it, and every command runs standalone whether it runs or not. The runtime is identified by the user, the canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) and the Git common directory, so two worktrees of one repository, or two users, never share one; the handshake compares the engine, build, protocol and schema as well and an attach from another engine is refused naming the field. Its endpoint is a Unix domain socket (Linux, macOS) of mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user (`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pose`, else `pose-runtime-<uid>` under the temporary directory, or `POSE_RUNTIME_DIR`), whose peer the operating system identifies before a byte is read; a link, a loose mode, another owner or a file that is not a socket is refused, and a socket nobody answers on is replaced. There is no TCP and no token. Slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers handshake, status and stop, confers no authority, signature or presence, and every restart has a new epoch, inheriting nothing. On Windows, which has no named-pipe implementation here, `status` reports `unsupported` and every command runs standalone. `status` exits 0 for running, standalone and unsupported and 1 for an incompatible runtime; `attach` also exits 1 when there is nothing to attach to. `--json` prints the document `pose.runtime.status/1`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017hw9R5mer3yKodG11rpkGQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
