ommand":"cd /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1986613151/worktree && pose surface-check --spec pose-optional-worktree-runtime --strict; echo \"exit=$?\"","timeout":300000,"description":"Run the strict surface check for the spec"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjkJ8BRupZ9mez8y2Wqgch","tool_input":{"command":"pose assess design --spec pose-optional-worktree-runtime --json","timeout":300000,"description":"Run the design assessment for the spec"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EGo5J5oi2rQ6GGVFKWjWCF","tool_input":{"command":"pose suggest review --path pose-mcp","timeout":300000,"description":"Ask POSE for review suggestions on pose-mcp"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01J5uN1vcJ8JHx8Bc1fMP4kY","tool_input":{"command":"pose assess discover --component pose-mcp","timeout":300000,"description":"Run component discovery assessment for pose-mcp"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":30,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving this change. All six defects I found are low severity, and each is recorded as a follow-up with an action, owner and review date.\n\n**decision: approved**\n\n**What I could run:** The profile let me run `pose artifact-check --strict` and `pose surface-check --strict`. It refused `pose assess design`, `pose assess discover`, `pose suggest review` and `git diff`. I read every changed implementation file, plus the spec, the ADR amendment, the four manual copies and the matrix entry. For build and test results I relied on the sealed evidence.\n\n## Tool results\n- **artifact-check:** passed, with warnings only. All of them are \"orphan\" provenance warnings on paths outside this change; there were no errors. One thing to note: it reported `change_set=cs-32ce227878cc` with head `45a9c798…`, while the brief names `cs-907a89218d5b` and head `db3aeda8`. I couldn't run `git log` to explain the difference.\n- **surface-check:** passed. 1 target, 200 results, 0 findings.\n\n## Criteria\n| criterion | result | evidence and reasoning |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | **Verified:** the peer uid is checked by the OS at `peercred_linux.go:18-36`, and directory and socket ownership, mode and type are checked at `runtime.go:156-185`. **Open assumptions, recorded as follow-ups:** no test with a second uid; no `vcs.modified` or capabilities in the identity; Windows. **Accepted risks:** endpoints in `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` or tmp can be wiped; users who share a uid share the endpoint. |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | One flock per endpoint, held for the life of the runtime (`runtime.go:236`). The endpoint is removed only if it is still this process's inode (`:259-263`). Concurrent-start and drain tests are sealed. Residual: K1, K3, K4. |\n| backend-contracts | passed | Additive only: a new `runtime` command (`cli.go:258`), the new `pose.runtime.status/1` document, and help in en and pt-BR. |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | Requests are capped at 64 KiB with a 5 s deadline (`runtime.go:367`). Typed errors: `ErrNoRuntime`, `IncompatibleError`, `UnsafeError`. Flags are validated, including a drain below 1 ms (`runtime_cmd.go:71`). |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | The new git caller is registered in `engine_reads_raw_history_test.go:45`; sealed evidence passes. |\n| backend-observability | passed | Mismatches are named field by field, the PID is returned, and drained and abandoned counts are reported. The detached serve's stderr is lost: this is J3, already a follow-up. |\n| compatibility | passed | Opt-in; no existing command changed behaviour; the four manual copies agree. |\n| correctness | passed | Sealed unit and integration evidence. Residual: K1–K4. |\n| design-causality | passed | D1 picks the smallest protected local endpoint: a 0600 socket, a 0700 directory and an OS peer check. The endpoint name comes from the location part, so a newer CLI finds the old process and the handshake refuses it by field. This matches the D1 falsifier. |\n| documentation | passed | `POSE.md:946` and its three copies match the code: paths, modes, exit codes, defaults. |\n| operability | passed | Hints name the process and remediation. Residual: K2. |\n| requirements | passed | Each of R1–R4 and R9 is traced to tests in the `optional-worktree-runtime-integration` matrix entry (`validation-matrix.json:2600-2613`). |\n| scope | passed | The runtime hosts no operation and confers no authority. R5–R8 are cleanly withdrawn to the two new specs. |\n| security | passed | Symlinks are refused because both checks use Lstat. A pre-created tmp directory or a squatted socket is refused; the worst outcome is a denial of service that falls back to standalone. The client also checks the peer uid. No TCP, no token. |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | The minimal option (no runtime) cannot satisfy R1–R3. No speculative hosting: `Handler` is test-only. What would invalidate the choice: a named-pipe requirement on Windows. |\n\n**Structural fact SD-43b82275** (the ADR changed): maps to D1, because the 2026-11-09 amendment is D1's decision basis. R9 also requires that ADR to be resolved before start.\n\n## Defects (all low, all follow-ups)\n- **K1:** `runtime.go:316` / `:403`. The handler's context is never cancelled when a stop's drain deadline passes, and `wg.Wait()` waits without limit. So \"abandoned\" requests keep running and the process outlives the stop. This is bounded today because production has no `Handler` and built-in ops have a 5 s deadline. It must be fixed before the resident-cache slice hosts operations.\n- **K2:** `runtime_cmd.go:141` / `:170`. `restart` ignores `WaitReleased`'s false result. If that times out, it spawns a serve that loses the lock silently, then reports \"did not answer after it was started\" instead of \"the previous runtime still holds the endpoint\".\n- **K3:** `runtime.go:414`. The drain counts other stop or status connections as requests in flight. Two concurrent stops each report the other as drained or abandoned.\n- **K4:** `runtime.go:359`. The idle clock runs from the *start* of the last request, so a request longer than the idle timeout is followed by an immediate idle shutdown.\n- **K5:** `runtime_cmd_test.go:66-72`. The CLI test never covers the `incompatible` state or exit code 1 that the manual promises. Its `stops` and `ctx` variables are dead code, so the in-process serves are never cancelled if a step fails.\n- **K6:** `validation-matrix.json:2600` and spec line 95. The `GOOS=windows go build ./...` check the spec declares has no producer in the matrix and no sealed evidence. `peercred_darwin.go` is not exercised by any sealed evidence either.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"K1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\", \"line\": 316, \"summary\": \"A stop never cancels the handler context and run() waits on wg.Wait without bound, so abandoned requests keep running and the process outlives the stop; bounded today only because no Handler is set in production.\", \"action\": \"Cancel a per-runtime context when the drain deadline passes and bound the final wait before the resident-cache slice hosts operations.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"K2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 141, \"summary\": \"restart ignores WaitReleased's false result; on timeout it spawns a serve that loses the lock silently and reports 'did not answer after it was started' instead of naming the holder.\", \"action\": \"Fail the restart with the previous PID when WaitReleased returns false.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"K3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\", \"line\": 414, \"summary\": \"drain counts concurrent stop/status connections as requests in flight, so two concurrent stops each report the other as drained or abandoned.\", \"action\": \"Count only hosted operations in flight (not control ops) in the drain.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"K4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go\", \"line\": 359, \"summary\": \"The idle clock is set at the start of a request, not its end; a request longer than the idle timeout is followed by an immediate idle shutdown.\", \"action\": \"Refresh the last-activity time when a request finishes.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"K5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd_test.go\", \"line\": 66, \"summary\": \"The CLI test does not exercise the documented 'incompatible' state / exit 1 path, and its stops/ctx are dead code, so in-process serves are never cancelled on a failed step.\", \"action\": \"Add a CLI case against a runtime of another engine and cancel the in-process serves in cleanup.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"K6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\", \"line\": 2600, \"summary\": \"The spec's deterministic check 'GOOS=windows go build ./...' has no matrix producer or sealed evidence, and peercred_darwin.go is not exercised by sealed evidence.\", \"action\": \"Add a cross-build (windows, darwin) check to the matrix.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined peercred_linux.go:18-36, runtime.go:156-185 and the spec's known gaps and residual risks. Verified: OS peer-uid check, directory and socket ownership/mode/type checks, flock exclusivity. Unresolved and recorded as low follow-ups: no second-uid test, identity lacks vcs.modified/capabilities, Windows. Accepted risks: endpoint directory cleanup, shared-uid containers.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The per-endpoint flock (runtime.go:236) and the inode-guarded removal (runtime.go:259-263) are covered by TestConcurrentStartsLeaveOneRuntimeAndNoOneRemovesItsSocket and TestARuntimeThatOutlivesItsEndpointRemovesOnlyItsOwn under -race; residuals K1, K3, K4 are low follow-ups.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/help-lists-every-command-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The runtime command and the pose.runtime.status/1 document are additive; no existing CLI, file or MCP contract changes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Requests are bounded (64 KiB, 5 s deadline, runtime.go:367); typed ErrNoRuntime/IncompatibleError/UnsafeError; flags validated at runtime_cmd.go:60-85.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The new RawHistoryGit caller is registered in engine_reads_raw_history_test.go:45; the CLI dispatch is wired at cli.go:258.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Mismatch fields, PID, epoch and drained/abandoned counts are returned; the lost stderr of a detached serve is the existing follow-up J3.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined cli.go help (en/pt-BR) and the four POSE.md copies: the command is opt-in and additive and no other command changes; concluded compatible.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Functional and negative paths (stale, unsafe, incompatible, no runtime) pass in sealed tests; residual low defects K1-K4 are follow-ups.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-ed004a44ddaaa4bf\", \"rationale\": \"D1 selects a 0600 Unix socket in a 0700 directory with an OS peer check and a location-only endpoint name, so a newer CLI finds the old process and is refused by field, which addresses R1/R2 and the D1 falsifier; the lifecycle addresses R3, ErrNoRuntime/standalone addresses R4.\", \"mappings\": [{\"delta\": \"SD-43b82275\", \"basis\": \"D1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR's 2026-11-09 amendment (transport, identity, slicing) is the decision basis D1 cites; R9 requires it to be resolved before start.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Compared POSE.md:946 and its three copies with runtime.go and runtime_cmd.go: paths, modes, defaults (5s drain, 30m idle) and exit codes match.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the hints in runtime_cmd.go:139 and :186: they name the PID and the remediation; K2 (restart timeout message) is a low follow-up.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/trace-test-refs-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Each of R1-R4 and R9 traces to tests that exist and run in the optional-worktree-runtime-integration matrix entry (validation-matrix.json:2600-2613).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the changed files against the spec's artifacts: the runtime hosts no operation (Handler nil in production) and confers no authority; R5-R8 are withdrawn to their own specs; surface-check found 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the Lstat checks (symlink refused), owner/mode checks, peer uid on both ends, no TCP or token, and squatting of the tmp fallback (refused, leaves standalone); concluded the authority boundaries hold.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-ed004a44ddaaa4bf\", \"rationale\": \"The minimal option (no runtime) cannot satisfy R1-R3; the implementation adds no hosted operation or cache (Handler is test-only), and the condition that invalidates it is a Windows named-pipe requirement, recorded as a follow-up.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-optional-worktree-runtime --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Warnings only (orphan provenance on paths outside this change); no errors.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-ed004a44ddaaa4bf\", \"rationale\": \"Running it was refused by this profile; the sealed structure result is cited.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; running it was refused by this review profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; not run in this profile; integration was judged from the sealed integration evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; not run in this profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the recorded attestation of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; running it was refused by this review profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\", \"rationale\": \"Also ran pose surface-check --spec pose-optional-worktree-runtime --strict: 1 target, 200 results, 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed strict validation evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed strict validation evidence for pose-mcp, including the runtime's -race integration check.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1381,"type":"result","duration_ms":346324,"uuid":"ce4dc3dc-69a9-4f1a-b402-24c1dc70888b","ttft_stream_ms":985,"time_to_request_ms":46,"first_content_frame_ms":985,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":38,"outputTokens":18960,"cacheReadInputTokens":1014273,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66954,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1178386,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":8375,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":66954,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-04T10:05:09.044Z"}
